Carafe Lab: the control channel records frames: `record <folder> <count>` saves each of the next `count` pictures
the renderer presents, in a row and at the screen's size, as `frame-0000.png` and on into the folder. Each picture
is taken the way `screenshot` takes one, and the next is asked for before the last is written, so no presented frame
is skipped. Eden answers `recording <count>`, or `error idle` when no software runs.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

